            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThe `grep_live` picker indeed doesn't respect Neovim's 'ignorecase' and 'smartcase' because it uses output of `rg` as is. The idea is to customize CLI tool directly.\n\nInitial implementation contained `--smart-case` by default, but it was removed in f39a455770aefdecda114370784c7dd7f9f7bf74 . The problem with including `rg` flags/options in `grep_live` command is that they take precedence over user's config.\n\nThat said, now that I am thinking about it, maybe forcing `--ignore-case` or `--smart-case` depending on Neovim's options might be a good idea. I'll have to think about it a bit more.",
